## Summary

Implemented **`DET.HASH.MARKERS`** as a deterministic DOM marker check, registered it in the blender map, and added unit tests. Shell commands were not available in this session, so you should run verification locally (below).

### What changed

**1. `design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-hash-markers.check.js`**

Replaced the no-op stub with a check that reads `metrics.ksVisualHashReport` (from `lib/dom-metrics.js` crawl) via `ksVisualHashReportFromMetrics()`. It flags:

| Signal | Severity | Meaning |
|--------|----------|---------|
| `invalidRaw` | minor | Value is not exactly three ASCII letters |
| `mismatches` | minor | `hash` and `data-ks-hash` differ on the same node |
| `incompleteMarkers` | warn | Only one of the two attributes is present |
